---
source: worktree/cli/tests/list_table.rs
expression: "labeled(vec![(\"plain\".into(),\nunlinked(\"/code/wts/plain\", Some(\"feat/plain\"))),\n(\"spaces in the path\".into(), unlinked(\"/code/wts/my work\", None)),\n(\"a single quote in the path\".into(), unlinked(\"/code/wts/it's\", None)),\n(\"a PowerShell quote in the path\".into(),\nunlinked(\"/code/wts/it\\u{2019}s\", None)),\n(\"shell metacharacters\".into(), unlinked(\"/code/wts/$(rm -rf ~);x\", None)),\n(\"a leading dash\".into(), unlinked(\"/code/wts/-n\", None)),])"
---
## plain
 - plain: its .git file is missing;  wt remove feat/plain  removes it.


## spaces in the path
 - my work: its .git file is missing;  wt remove 'my work'  removes it.


## a single quote in the path
 - it's: its .git file is missing; wt remove removes it. No name selects it for wt remove: it's can't be typed the same way in every shell.


## a PowerShell quote in the path
 - it’s: its .git file is missing; wt remove removes it. No name selects it for wt remove: it’s can't be typed the same way in every shell.


## shell metacharacters
 - $(rm -rf ~);x: its .git file is missing;  wt remove '$(rm -rf ~);x'  removes it.


## a leading dash
 - -n: its .git file is missing; wt remove removes it. No name selects it for wt remove: -n can't be typed the same way in every shell.
